<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-10-27T08:56:34+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:56:34 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Afghan returnees face police raids, arbitrary detention in Pakistan's KP after emergency: Report]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135223253.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Afghan nationals deported from Pakistan have alleged arbitrary arrests, midnight raids and extortion in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa following the imposition of governor’s rule and a state of emergency by the Shehbaz Sharif government. Returnees said police were demanding bribes for release. Nearly 27,000 Afghan refugees have returned through Torkham in three months, amid resettlement efforts.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/afghan-returnees-face-police-raids-arbitrary-detention-in-pakistans-kp-after-emergency-report/articleshow/135223253.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/afghan-returnees-face-police-raids-arbitrary-detention-in-pakistans-kp-after-emergency-report/articleshow/135223253.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T08:29:28+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135223284,imgsize-1099766.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California court revives $1M lawsuit over 3-year delay in approving a homeowner’s second dwelling]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135219344.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a legal battle, California resident Wei Shi has taken the City of Palos Verdes Estates to court, claiming excessive delays in the approval of his accessory dwelling unit application. Shi asserts that the city violated state law’s requirements for prompt reviews. Thanks to a favorable ruling from an appeals court, his lawsuit is back on track, seeking over $1 million in damages for these holdups.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2020-a-california-homeowner-applied-to-build-a-second-dwelling-on-his-property-but-says-the-city-delayed-approval-for-over-three-years-causing-more-than-1-million-in-losses-an-october-23-court-revived-his-lawsuit/articleshow/135219344.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2020-a-california-homeowner-applied-to-build-a-second-dwelling-on-his-property-but-says-the-city-delayed-approval-for-over-three-years-causing-more-than-1-million-in-losses-an-october-23-court-revived-his-lawsuit/articleshow/135219344.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T08:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135219371,imgsize-1702205.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Trump’s approval ratings slightly recover after record low last week: Report]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135222555.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[US President Donald Trump’s approval rating has increased to 32 percent, showing a small recovery. In contrast, a recent poll indicates that registered voters prefer Democrats over Republicans by 47 percent to 36 percent. As the midterm elections approach, voter enthusiasm appears to be higher among Democrats compared to Republicans. Additionally, voters’ views on economic management have shifted, favoring Democrats slightly over Republicans.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-mid-term-elections/news/trumps-approval-ratings-slightly-recover-after-record-low-last-week-report/articleshow/135222555.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-mid-term-elections/news/trumps-approval-ratings-slightly-recover-after-record-low-last-week-report/articleshow/135222555.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T07:29:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135222587,imgsize-97216.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Can Netanyahu survive another storm? Israel votes after Oct 7, Gaza and Iran wars]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135222527.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/can-netanyahu-survive-another-storm-israel-votes-after-october-7-gaza-and-iran-wars/articleshow/135222527.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/can-netanyahu-sur